description:
5th recording of this individual; 
this Brewer's Sparrow is responding to playback of Clay-colored by giving a few songs with more typical Brewer's phrases, and circling us, then returned to its variant song (we never did play back Brewer's to it);
variant song type (short and simple) from what I know

singing from top of 2 and 3 m stunted conifers in treeline scrub; in response to playback, but not very energetic about its response, and foraging on ground at end of recording (but very responsive physically--immediately came close); soft song at close range;
apparent call note at 0:43;
Individual No 1, 2nd recording of it

habitat:Amazônia - Terra Firme;
